# Blink
# Level 1 - Basics
#
# The hello-world of hardware: the board's own LED turns on and off.
# You learn: naming a pin, 'as output', 'every' and toggle().
# You need: nothing extra - the LED is already on the board (next to pin 13 on an Uno).

board uno

led = pin LED as output            # LED is the built-in LED; you could write pin 13 instead

every 500 ms:                      # twice a second...
    led.toggle()                   # ...switch the LED: on if it was off, off if it was on
